-- title:
--   A Lubin–Tate coordinate W₀[[X]] → R for a lift of F₀
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $W_0$ a complete discrete valuation domain (complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, equipped with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, that is: with the ambient ideal taken to be $\bot$, there is a unit $u \in k[[X]]$ with $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ q = u \cdot F_0.\mathrm{drinfeldDivisor}\ q\ 0\ 0$. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with a surjective $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which agrees with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$, and let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ whose push-forward along $\mathrm{res}_R$ is $F_0$ (i.e. $F_0$'s two-variable series is the image of $F$'s). Let $F^u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[X]]$ whose push-forward along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$. Assume the Lubin–Tate universal property for $F^u$ over Artinian bases: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjective $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ of kernel the maximal ideal agreeing with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on $W_0$, and every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ with push-forward $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ for which the push-forward $G'$ of $F^u$ along $\varphi$ admits an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi : G' \to G$ (a power series with zero constant term and unit linear term satisfying the homomorphism identity) whose series reduces to $X$ under $\mathrm{res}_T$, i.e. the $n$-th coefficient maps to $1$ for $n = 1$ and to $0$ otherwise. The conclusion asserts the existence (not uniqueness) of a $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[X]] \to R$ with $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ and $\varphi(X)$ in the maximal ideal of $R$, together with a formal group law $F'$ over $R$ that is the push-forward of $F^u$ along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism $\psi : F' \to F$ whose series reduces to $X$ in the same sense.
--
--   This is the passage from the Lubin–Tate universal property over Artinian bases to the classification of a lift over a complete Noetherian local base: the resulting map $\varphi$ is the Lubin–Tate coordinate of the deformation $F$, exhibiting $R$ as receiving the universal deformation ring $W_0[[X]]$. It is used in the study of deformation rings carrying Drinfeld level structure, in particular in the proof that such a ring is regular of Krull dimension two, and in the local analysis of completions of modular curves with full level structure.
